        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "Static scope review, 2026-10-25 UTC. SHA-256 verified; complete 1,173-byte Bash script, 27 lines, six command-availability branches and six closing fi statements. An isolated bash -n parse-only check succeeds; no script command was executed. All branches select the same reverse-shell callback, 68.183.68.82:5656, using available shell/network tools and redirected standard streams. The sample references revshells.com, a dual-use generation tool; that site is not itself a malware IOC. URLhaus payload lookup already associates this exact hash with delivery record https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/url/3878283/ (service-reported status online during review). No delivery or callback connection was attempted and no duplicate URL submission was made. The code proves a reverse-shell capability; attribution, authorization of use, and an actual compromised-host session are not established by this script alone. Retained under a review hold rather than assigned an unsupported malware-family label."
